<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Sage foreign issue raises final $45 mln.</title>
<headline>Sage foreign issue raises final $45 mln.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African insurance group Sage Group Ltd said on Monday its recent share issue to European investors had been completed, raising a final $45 million to help the expansion of its U.S. life assurance activities.  </p>
<p>The issue raised $40 million initially and a further $5 million was placed under an option by the managers to the issue, Nomura International, HSBC Investment Bank and Merrill Lynch International.</p>
<p>Trading in the new redeemable preference shares will begin on the Luxembourg Stock Exchange on July 1.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
